WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.772
- So unlike many of you here,

00:00:09.772 --> 00:00:12.780
I am not technology savvy person.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.153
However, I'm just very practical person.

00:00:16.153 --> 00:00:19.256
So today I simply would like to share

00:00:19.256 --> 00:00:23.876
one of the features I found
very useful and practical.

00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:25.983
That is Canvas Modules.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.090
Okay, so builders often time to say

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:34.880
don't even try to build a
house without blueprints, okay?

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.610
So blueprints, the
general definition of it

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.361
is a set of construction
or working drawings

00:00:42.361 --> 00:00:45.890
that define all the constructions specs

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:49.040
of a residential house such as dimensions,

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.693
materials, layouts, installation
method and techniques.

00:00:55.282 --> 00:00:57.630
So in the same context,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.300
I think teaching and learning modules

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.000
means detailed lesson plans
that presents assessments,

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.469
assignments, projects, homework,

00:01:08.469 --> 00:01:12.530
learning activities,
presentations, resources,

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:16.210
even timeline and expected
or final outcomes.

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.110
So basically you can put every ingredients

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.928
into this Canvas Modules
about your course.

00:01:22.928 --> 00:01:26.390
Therefore I think Canvas
Modules merely functions

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.373
as blueprints of your course curriculum.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.650
As you see here, you can
organize your materials

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:38.893
by each category.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:43.763
So even resources, you can
put all course resources here.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.942
And this is the big categories.

00:01:47.942 --> 00:01:50.880
You can organize your course contents

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.630
by unit and time or both.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.720
So each of big categories

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.480
can have more detailed ingredients.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.037
So you can put, as I said here,

00:02:02.037 --> 00:02:07.037
assignment, presentations, or
test quizzes and everything.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.790
So again, why do I use Canvas Modules?

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:15.760
I said it's easy to use,

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.070
and it's a clear communication tool,

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.970
communication tool
between me and my students

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.350
and my colleagues and my teaching fellows.

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:29.350
Especially for multi-section
and team-teaching setting.

00:02:29.813 --> 00:02:33.173
Also this is great tool
for course organize.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:40.730
So I am course head and
coordinator of the program,

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.800
so through these Canvas Modules

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.860
I can really keep curricular consistency

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.783
and pedagogical alignment.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:54.472
And also great tool for training my TFs,

00:02:54.472 --> 00:02:56.870
and often times they call,

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.140
what do I teach, and how do I teach,

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:03.960
and I clearly directed them
to these Canvas Modules.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.810
So through these Canvas Modules, again,

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:11.310
I can keep my course very
transparent to my students

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.550
and colleagues and teaching fellows.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.785
So after all,

00:03:15.785 --> 00:03:20.513
the modules can function
as your course portfolio.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.690
So these are the frequent
asked questions I get.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.080
I'm sure you guys get
these kind of questions

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.880
from your students or teaching
fellows or colleagues.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.380
So where should I upload my assignments?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:38.960
Students still ask the questions.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.543
Surprisingly, some of
students don't even read

00:03:41.543 --> 00:03:45.071
the course syllabus until
the end of a semester.

00:03:45.071 --> 00:03:48.330
What should I cover
next week in section X?

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.430
TFs can ask these questions.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.840
And then what do you teach in this course?

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.790
Well, often times it's
your colleagues ask you.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.310
You can now answer by
saying I teach very well,

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.490
and I do a lot of different
stuff in my class.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:06.198
Simply visualize what
you do with your students

00:04:06.198 --> 00:04:09.470
in the course through Canvas Modules.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.980
These questions go on and on and on,

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.980
so now you know my answer
is, you can answer for me,

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:23.680
through Canvas Modules,
that is correct, yes.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.890
So this is great tool
and very easy to utilize.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:33.070
So please use them as much as possible

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:36.776
and I get great support from Christine

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:41.776
and Kimberly and all campus colleagues.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:43.643
That's it.

00:04:46.221 --> 00:04:48.425
(applause)

00:04:48.425 --> 00:04:50.800
Too early?
- [Woman] Questions?

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:51.633
- Questions?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.420
How many of you use Canvas Modules?

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.253
Ah, see.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.759
You can add some anecdote, yeah?

00:05:08.759 --> 00:05:11.560
- [Woman] Do your students ever,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.170
at the beginning of the term
or even throughout the term,

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:16.210
forget that you're using the modules?

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:17.680
I know this is something
that I struggle with.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.200
Like, I have to tell
my students repeatedly,

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.200
over and over again.

00:05:21.094 --> 00:05:22.524
Oh where is this resource?

00:05:22.524 --> 00:05:23.430
It's in the module, look in the modules.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:26.020
How do you combat that in class?

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:26.853
- So beginning of the semester,

00:05:27.809 --> 00:05:29.030
I clearly say everything
is in the modules,

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.920
and then I enforce them every day,

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.750
did you check Canvas Modules?

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:38.543
And then, first week or so,
they all get settled, yeah.

00:05:40.795 --> 00:05:42.793
- [Woman] I also find it helpful

00:05:42.793 --> 00:05:45.105
that if you don't just
put it in the module,

00:05:45.105 --> 00:05:48.040
but if you, thank you, if you assign...

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.300
Like for example, for mine,

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.890
I organize everything by chapter.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:53.670
So they will look for that particular item

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.180
in modules in that chapter.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.610
But otherwise, you're right.

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.470
I mean, I can't keep my quizzes in quizzes

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.020
because nobody will find them

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.840
or else they will take the wrong one,

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.740
of course, we know that problem.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.670
But the linear organization week by week

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.770
I highly recommend organizing
either on calendar basis,

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.410
like how your syllabus
runs week one, week two,

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.533
or in our case, it's by chapter.

00:06:18.485 --> 00:06:21.830
- [Woman] Another option is to use pages.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:24.860
On the first page you
will just have a link

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:28.373
to the right modules, that
way they won't be confused.

00:06:34.427 --> 00:06:37.260
- Any other questions or comments?

00:06:41.154 --> 00:06:42.407
All right, thank you.

00:06:43.277 --> 00:06:46.194
- [Timberley] Great, thank you so much.

